This package includes material from the following projects.

src/library/volviewPresets.ts
  The transfer function presets of VolView (src/vtk/MedicalColorPresets.json), copied as data.
  https://github.com/Kitware/VolView
  Copyright Kitware, Inc. Apache License 2.0.

src/library/colorMaps.ts
  Colour maps from vtk.js (Sources/Rendering/Core/ColorTransferFunction/ColorMaps.json), resampled.
  https://github.com/Kitware/vtk-js
  Copyright (c) 2016, Kitware Inc. BSD 3-Clause License.
  viridis, magma, inferno and plasma are the matplotlib colour maps by Nathaniel J. Smith, Stefan van der Walt and
  Eric Firing, released as CC0: https://bids.github.io/colormap/

src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl
  volNoise: interleaved gradient noise, Jorge Jimenez, "Next Generation Post Processing in Call of Duty: Advanced
  Warfare", SIGGRAPH 2014.
  The ray-box test, back-face ray setup and camera-inside handling follow the three.js volume examples
  (examples/webgl_volume_cloud.html) and VolumeNodeMaterial, https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js, MIT License.

src/loaders/NRRDLoadPlugin.ts, src/VolumeData.ts
  Use three.js NRRDLoader and Volume (examples/jsm), https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js, MIT License.

src/derived/EmptySpaceMap.ts, src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl
  Empty space skipping with a Chebyshev distance map follows the method of L. J. Deakin and M. A. Knackstedt,
  "Accelerated volume rendering with Chebyshev distance maps", SIGGRAPH Asia 2019 Technical Briefs (no code copied).
